                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle -,-\rangle
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathfrak{g} \otimes \mathfrak{g}
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since this is non-degenerate, we may equivalently think of this as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathfrak{g} \simeq \mathfrak{g}^*
          %p
            that identifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            underlying the Lie algebra with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
          %h3#TheCoadjointOrbitAndTheCosetSpaceAndFlagManifold The coadjoint orbit and the coset space/ flag manifold
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbits"} coadjoint orbits
