                  %strong 73
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/bull/1967-73-05/S0002-9904-1967-11829-9/S0002-9904-1967-11829-9.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Polarization and unitary representations of solvable Lie groups
                %strong 14
                (1971), 255–354,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=293012"} MR293012
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF01389744"} doi
            %li#GrahamVogan
              %p
                W. Graham,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Vogan"} David Vogan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric quantization for nilpotent coadjoint orbits
            %li#Vogan99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Vogan"}> David Vogan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The method of coadjoint orbits for real reductive groups
          %p
            Discussion with an eye towards application in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            and in particular for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop"} Wilson loop
            observables in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %ul
            %li#Witten89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , p. 22, 23 of
              %em Quantum Field Theory and the Jones Polynomial
              Commun. Math. Phys. 121 (3) (1989) 351–399. MR0990772 (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104178138"}> project EUCLID
              )
          %p is in section 4 of
          %ul
            %li#Beasley11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Beasley"}> Chris Beasley
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Localization for Wilson Loops in Chern-Simons Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chern-Simons Gauge Theory: 20 Years After
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 50
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2687"} arXiv:0911.2687
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.intlpress.com/site/pub/pages/books/items/00000258/index.php"} ISBN:9780821853535
          %p referring to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shmuel+Elitzur"}> Shmuel Elitzur
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"} Nathan Seiberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Remarks on the Canonical Quantization of the Chern-Simons-Witten Theory
          %p
            A program of applying the orbit method to real nilpotent orbits of real semisimple Lie groups (closely related to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+via+the+A-model"} quantization via the A-model
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Ranee Brylinski,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric Quantization of Real Minimal Nilpotent Orbits
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9811033"} arXiv:math/9811033
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %em>
                      Quantization of the 4-dimensional nilpotent orbit of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi SL
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 3
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(3,\mathbb{R})
                    , Canad. J. Math. 49(1997), 916-943 (
                    %a{:href => "http://cms.math.ca/cjm/a148867"}> web
                    )
                %li
                  %p
                    %em Instantons and Kähler Geometry of Nilpotent Orbits
                    (
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9811032"}> arXiv:math/9811032
                    )
          %p
            Discussion of the orbit method in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+induction"} Dirac induction
            is in
          %ul
            %li#HFT
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loop+Groups+and+Twisted+K-Theory"} Loop Groups and Twisted K-Theory
            %li#Hochs12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Hochs"}> Peter Hochs
                , section 2.2 of
                %em Quantisation of presymplectic manifolds, K-theory and group representations
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.0107"}> arXiv:1211.0107
                )
          %p
            The generalization of this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Ganter12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nora+Ganter"}> Nora Ganter
              ,
              %em The elliptic Weyl character formula
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.0528"}> arXiv:1206.0528
              )
          %p
            Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            is discussed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Gijs M. Tuynman,
                %em Geometric Quantization of Superorbits: a Case Study
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0901.1811"}> arXiv:0901.1811
                )
            %li
              %p
                Alexander Alldridge, Joachim Hilgert, Tilmann Wurzbacher,
                %em Superorbits
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.04375"}> arXiv:1502.04375
                )
          %p
            A generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-representations"} 2-representations
            is proposed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Bartlett"}> Bruce Bartlett
              ,
              %em On unitary 2-representations of finite groups and topological quantum field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0901.3975"}> arXiv:0901.3975
              )
          %p
            The above discussion of the interpretation of the orbit method in terms of higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            appears in
          %ul
            %li#FSS
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/A+higher+stacky+perspective+on+Chern-Simons+theory"} A higher stacky perspective on Chern-Simons theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Mathematical Aspects of Quantum Field Theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.2580"} arXiv:1301.2580
        .revisedby
